<h1>Scorecard QA Checklist — Pre-Submit Review</h1>
<p>Complete before submitting scorecard to the debrief channel.</p>
<h2>Evidence Completeness</h2>
<p>For each competency scored:</p>
<ul><li>[ ] At least one specific STAR example is documented (Situation + Action + Result minimum)</li><li>[ ] No impression-only language (&quot;seemed confident&quot;, &quot;good communicator&quot;, &quot;liked them&quot;)</li><li>[ ] Every score &gt;= 4 has a verbatim quote or concrete described action as evidence</li><li>[ ] Every score &lt;= 2 has a specific missing component documented (e.g., &quot;No quantified Result&quot;)</li></ul>
<h2>Protected-Class Review</h2>
<ul><li>[ ] No mention of age, family status, pregnancy, religion, disability, nationality</li><li>[ ] No note about accent, communication style, or &quot;fit&quot; without behavioral evidence</li></ul>
<h2>Hypothetical Acceptance Check</h2>
<ul><li>[ ] No score based on hypothetical answers (&quot;I would...&quot;, &quot;I generally...&quot;)</li><li>[ ] All scored examples are confirmed past behavior (&quot;I did...&quot;, &quot;Last year...&quot;, etc.)</li></ul>
<h2>Pronoun Accuracy</h2>
<ul><li>[ ] For any score on Action: candidate used &quot;I&quot; statements, not only &quot;we&quot;</li><li>[ ] If &quot;we&quot; was dominant: probing question was asked and individual contribution documented</li></ul>
<h2>Completeness</h2>
<ul><li>[ ] All competencies have a score AND an evidence note</li><li>[ ] Hire/No Hire recommendation is present</li><li>[ ] Key strengths section has at least one specific example</li><li>[ ] Areas of concern section is filled if score &lt;= 3 on any competency</li></ul>
<h2>Submission Rule</h2>
<ul><li>[ ] Scorecard submitted BEFORE reading any other interviewer's feedback</li><li>[ ] Score is not changed after seeing peer scores (unless new information arises in debrief)</li></ul>
</body></html>
